&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years’ experience:&lt;/strong&gt; In-house technical recruiting background (ideally combined with agency experience), with a track record of scaling engineering or product teams in fast-paced tech environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical literacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Clear understanding of tech stacks, engineering roles (backend, frontend, full-stack, DevOps, data), and technical profile evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outbound sourcing ability:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled in technical candidate sourcing beyond LinkedIn (such as GitHub, Stack Overflow, X, and open-source communities).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to consult, align, and work with Engineering Managers and Product leaders on hiring strategy and candidate calibration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tool &amp;amp; metrics focus:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with AI tools and recruitment platforms, paired with experience using hiring metrics to monitor funnel performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to convey technical concepts, engineering culture, and product vision to passive candidates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract &amp;amp; location fit:&lt;/strong&gt; Availability for an up to 12-month Fixed-Term Contract (FTC), based in London with the ability to work from the Old Street office 3 days a week.&lt;/li&gt;
